{"name":"Art Academia","title":"Art Academia","revision":230396,"url":"https://aesthetics.fandom.com/wiki/Art_Academia","retrieved":"2026-09-06","license":"CC BY-SA","licenseUrl":"https://www.fandom.com/licensing","language":"en","blocks":[{"kind":"paragraph","text":"Art Academia is an Academic aesthetic centered around the creation and enjoyment of art, including sculpture, painting, sketch, doodling, photography, and calligraphy. It is similar to Light Academia and Dark Academia in its value of studying, dedicated practice of learned interests, 18-19th century-inspired aesthetics, and architecture, but is unique in focusing primarily on the visual arts."},{"kind":"heading","text":"Visuals"},{"kind":"paragraph","text":"Art Academia is centered primarily around the visual arts, and as such is primarily a visual aesthetic. Color schemes are generally warm and neutral with bright colors either scattered throughout or focused to draw the viewers' attention."},{"kind":"paragraph","text":"Popular visuals include (but may not be limited to):"},{"kind":"list","text":"Sculpture Pre-modern sculpture Greek Roman"},{"kind":"list","text":"Sketches"},{"kind":"list","text":"Doodles"},{"kind":"list","text":"Diagrams"},{"kind":"list","text":"Calligraphy"},{"kind":"list","text":"Cartography Stylized cartography"},{"kind":"list","text":"Photographs"},{"kind":"list","text":"Architecture Places of learning Universities Museums"},{"kind":"heading","text":"Courses"},{"kind":"paragraph","text":"People who partake in this aesthetic typically study at a college or a university, and therefore have to choose from a variety of subjects. Students choose specific courses to suit their future career or personal interest. Some of them include:"},{"kind":"list","text":"Ceramics"},{"kind":"list","text":"Drawing"},{"kind":"list","text":"Colour theory"},{"kind":"list","text":"Perspective"},{"kind":"list","text":"Graphic design"},{"kind":"list","text":"History of art"},{"kind":"list","text":"Painting"},{"kind":"list","text":"Print making"},{"kind":"list","text":"Sculpture"},{"kind":"list","text":"Visual arts"},{"kind":"list","text":"Watercolor"},{"kind":"list","text":"Animation"},{"kind":"list","text":"Typography"},{"kind":"list","text":"World arts"},{"kind":"heading","text":"Activities"},{"kind":"paragraph","text":"Generally, all activities are somehow related to learning about art or interacting with it. Of course, it can be done in different forms, such as:"},{"kind":"list","text":"Walking through museums and galleries"},{"kind":"list","text":"Attending life drawing classes"},{"kind":"list","text":"Drawing in general"},{"kind":"list","text":"Creating art pieces (e.g. charcoal portraits)"},{"kind":"list","text":"Writing creatively"},{"kind":"list","text":"Admiring architecture and the ageless faces of statues"},{"kind":"list","text":"Reading books"},{"kind":"list","text":"Listening to music"},{"kind":"list","text":"Journaling"},{"kind":"list","text":"Playing music"},{"kind":"list","text":"Painting"},{"kind":"list","text":"Attending plays"},{"kind":"list","text":"Attending the theater"},{"kind":"list","text":"Analyzing films"},{"kind":"list","text":"Photography"},{"kind":"heading","text":"Fashion"},{"kind":"list","text":"Collared shirts with puffy sleeves"},{"kind":"list","text":"Berets"},{"kind":"list","text":"Oxfords"},{"kind":"list","text":"Corduroy"},{"kind":"list","text":"Overalls"},{"kind":"list","text":"Braids, ponytails and messy buns"},{"kind":"list","text":"Wool sweaters"},{"kind":"list","text":"Loose t-shirts"},{"kind":"list","text":"Earthy colors"},{"kind":"list","text":"Paint stains on clothes"},{"kind":"heading","text":"Media"},{"kind":"paragraph","text":"All of the media associated with Art Academia are either about artists or are a part of art cinema."},{"kind":"heading","text":"Films"},{"kind":"list","text":"Painters Painting: The New York Art Scene (1940-1970)"},{"kind":"list","text":"Visit to Picasso (1949)"},{"kind":"list","text":"Orpheus (1950)"},{"kind":"list","text":"The Agony and the Ecstasy (1965)"},{"kind":"list","text":"Persona (1966)"},{"kind":"list","text":"Daisies (1966)"},{"kind":"list","text":"Golub: Late Works are the Catastrophes (1988)"},{"kind":"list","text":"La Belle Noiseuse (1991)"},{"kind":"list","text":"What Remains: The Life and Work of Sally Mann (2005)"},{"kind":"list","text":"Seraphine (2008)"},{"kind":"list","text":"Dorothea Lange: Grab a Hunk of Lightning (2014)"},{"kind":"list","text":"Loving Vincent (2017)"},{"kind":"list","text":"KUSAMA - INFINITY (2018)"},{"kind":"list","text":"Museum Town (2019)"},{"kind":"heading","text":"Anime"},{"kind":"list","text":"Love Through a Prism (2026)"},{"kind":"heading","text":"Music"},{"kind":"paragraph","text":"All of the following artists contribute to Art Academia:"},{"kind":"heading","text":"Artists"},{"kind":"list","text":"Cigarettes After Sex"},{"kind":"list","text":"Crisaunt"},{"kind":"list","text":"Cults"},{"kind":"list","text":"Dayglow"},{"kind":"list","text":"FINNEAS"},{"kind":"list","text":"Frank Ocean"},{"kind":"list","text":"Harmless"},{"kind":"list","text":"JAWNY"},{"kind":"list","text":"Joji"},{"kind":"list","text":"Llusion"},{"kind":"list","text":"M83"},{"kind":"list","text":"Mac DeMarco"},{"kind":"list","text":"Matt Maltese"},{"kind":"list","text":"Men I Trust"},{"kind":"list","text":"MGMT"},{"kind":"list","text":"Mild High Club"},{"kind":"list","text":"mxmtoon"},{"kind":"list","text":"Still Woozy"},{"kind":"list","text":"Strawberry Guy"},{"kind":"list","text":"Troye Sivan"}],"contentStatus":"full-source","images":[{"src":"https://static.wikia.nocookie.net/aesthetics/images/2/23/Art.PNG/revision/latest?cb=20200504145457","caption":"Art","source":"https://aesthetics.fandom.com/wiki/File:Art.PNG","remote":true,"local":"images/detail/0057-1.webp","localAvailable":true},{"src":"https://static.wikia.nocookie.net/aesthetics/images/6/6c/Tumblr_9b7534d705c5db738b3e89dff66db95c_c639aeb1_640.jpg/revision/latest?cb=20200701233431","caption":"Art Academia · Visual reference 02","source":"https://aesthetics.fandom.com/wiki/File:Tumblr_9b7534d705c5db738b3e89dff66db95c_c639aeb1_640.jpg","remote":true,"local":"images/detail/0057-2.webp","localAvailable":true}]}